The rugs are brightly decorated in abstract patterns.	這些地毯以鮮豔的抽象花紋裝飾著。
There are four, plain walls forming this enclosed yard.	四面樸素的牆，圍成這座封閉的庭院。
The ground is bone dry and covered with a pale sandy soil.	地面乾涸龜裂，覆著一層淺色的沙土。
The most powerful smell here is that of the qahwah, which is both bitter and oddly pleasant.	此處最濃烈的氣味來自卡瓦，苦澀卻又帶著一股奇異的怡人香氣。
Can you not tell when you are on your own two feet?	你難道連自己是不是站著都分不清？
It would be better to pay attention, Arthur.	你最好專心點，亞瑟。
That would be a silly thing to carry about with you in the desert.	帶著這東西走進沙漠，未免太蠢。
Al-Sirat has informed you that your mule is being cared for by Hazm.  When you leave, she will be there, as usual.	Al-Sirat 已告訴你，你的騾子由哈慈照料著。你離去時，她一如往常會在那裡等你。
It should be obvious that this scholar has no money.	顯而易見，這位學者身無分文。
Only by passing the tests of the Six Guardians will you eventually find the Grail.	唯有通過六位守護者的試煉，你才能終得聖杯。
Are you sure, Arthur?  The qahwah is a bit TOO invigorating.  I fear you may never sleep again.	你確定嗎，亞瑟？這卡瓦提神得有點過頭，我擔心你恐怕從此再也睡不著了。
I am sorry, my friend, there is no more.	抱歉，朋友，已經沒有了。
Thank you, I have had my fill.	多謝，我已經喝夠了。
Your cup is full, Arthur.	你的杯子已經滿了，亞瑟。
You ARE sitting, Arthur.	你已經坐著了，亞瑟。
Jerusalem lies northeast of Gaza, but you must pass through the desert to reach it.  And you cannot survive the heat of this desert unless you find water upon the way.	耶路撒冷位於加薩東北方，但你必須穿越沙漠才能抵達。若不能在途中尋得水源，你撐不過這片沙漠的酷熱。
Farewell.	珍重。
You must stand up before you can take your leave.	你得先起身，才能告辭離去。
My pardons, I have only qahwah for you.	恕我招待不周，我只有卡瓦能奉上。
In the name of the Goddess, I bid you welcome.	以女神之名，歡迎你的到來。
I am ready to answer what inquiries you put to me.  Think carefully and neglect nothing, for you will not see me again once you leave here.	我已備妥回答你的一切詢問。仔細思量，不要遺漏任何事，因為你一旦離開此處，便不會再見到我了。
When you leave here, he will lead you by secret paths away from Gaza to the edge of the desert that you must cross.	你離開此處時，他會引你走隱密的小徑，穿出加薩，直抵你必須橫越的那片沙漠邊緣。
To walk the path that leads to truth and knowledge is all that I desire.	行走在通往真理與知識的道路上，便是我唯一的心願。
I cannot accept such a gift, nor do I desire it.	這樣的餽贈，我既不能收下，也毫無所求。
I have no money, but there are merchants aplenty in Jerusalem.	我身無分文，但耶路撒冷不乏商賈。
I have little, and nothing I choose to sell.	我所有無多，也沒有什麼願意出售。
No words, however crude or foul, can affect me unless I allow it, which I shall not.	無論多麼粗鄙污穢的言語，都動搖不了我，除非我自己允許，而我絕不會如此。
I do not travel in the desert and cannot give you any directions, save that Jerusalem lies northeast of Gaza.  But beware, the way through the desert is devious.	我不曾涉足沙漠，無法為你指路，只知耶路撒冷位於加薩東北方。但要當心，穿越沙漠的路途詭譎多變。
Hazm will pass a well as he leads you from Gaza and there you may drink.  Beyond that, I cannot help you.	哈慈引你離開加薩時，會經過一口水井，你可在那裡飲水。除此之外，我便幫不上你了。
I have no waterskin to give you, I regret.	很遺憾，我沒有水袋可以給你。
I will not part with my carafe, nor would it serve your purpose.	我的水瓶我不會割捨，況且它也派不上你的用場。
I will not part with my qahwah cups and, delicate as they are, they would not endure your journey.	我的卡瓦杯我不會割捨，況且它們精巧易碎，禁不起你這趟旅程的顛簸。
I will not part with my bowl.  It is the only one I have.	我的碗我不會割捨，那是我僅有的一只。
I will not part with my rugs.  Indeed, what you see here is nearly all I possess.	我的地毯我不會割捨。說實話，你眼前所見，幾乎就是我的全部家當了。
Although many Muslims are tolerant of Christians, the mukhtar of Gaza delights in killing them, or anyone like them.	儘管許多穆斯林對基督徒相當包容，加薩的村長卻樂於殺害基督徒，或任何與他們相似之人。
There is no more qahwah.  You seem to have aquired a taste for it quite readily.	卡瓦已經沒有了。看來你很快便對它上了癮。
The carafe and the cups are for my qahwah.  Please help yourself.	這水瓶與杯子是用來盛我的卡瓦，請自行取用。
Qahwah is a hot drink made from brewing the roasted, crushed beans of the qahwah tree.	卡瓦是一種熱飲，以卡瓦樹烘焙、搗碎的豆子沖煮而成。
You may find it bitter, but it is most invigorating.	你或許會覺得它苦澀，但提神效果極佳。
You have eaten all the figs.	你已把無花果吃個精光。
In the bowl on the table are sweet figs that Hazm picked for me.  Please eat them, if you wish.	桌上碗裡是哈慈替我摘來的甜無花果，你若想吃，儘管取用。
I will show you the symbol again, if you will name the goddess whose symbol you wish to see.	你若說出想看哪位女神的標識，我便再展示給你看。
There is no symbol to see......yet.	眼下……還沒有標識可看。
He is a good boy and will be a fine scholar one day.	他是個好孩子，日後必成一位傑出的學者。
You need not fear for your mule.  Hazm loves animals and will take good care of her until you are ready to depart.	你不必為你的騾子擔心。哈慈喜愛動物，會妥善照顧她，直到你準備啟程為止。
Six Guardians stand between you and this sacred cup.  Six times you will be judged, weighed and tested.  They will be tests of mind, spirit and body.	六位守護者橫亙在你與這只聖杯之間。你將受六次評斷、衡量與試煉，考驗你的心智、心靈與體魄。
If you prevail, the Goddess will relinquish her guardianship of the sacred cup.  What you call the Holy Grail will pass into your hands and its powers of regeneration will be yours.	你若得勝，女神便會放下對這只聖杯的守護。你所稱的聖杯將落入你手中，其重生之力亦將歸你所有。
There are six you must pass.  I am the first.	你必須通過六位守護者，我是第一位。
There are always bandits, for there are always men of greed.	盜匪永遠都在，因為貪婪之人永遠都在。
To reach paradise, one must walk the razor-edged path of truth and purity.	欲達天堂，須行走於真理與純潔那條如刀鋒般的道路。
He who came before you searched long and far, yet he did not come here, though I sent Hazm with an invitation.	在你之前來尋訪的那位，找了許久、走了很遠，卻始終沒有來到此處，儘管我已派哈慈送去邀請。
I know nothing more of him save that he reached Jerusalem, but has not succeeded in his quest.	關於他，我只知他已抵達耶路撒冷，但尚未完成他的探尋。
He did not come to this land.	他並未來到這片土地。
The Goddess gave birth to the universe.  By many names and faces she is known.  As Virgin, Mother and Crone.  As Birth, Growth and Death.	女神孕育了宇宙。世人以諸多名號與面貌認識她：作為處女、母親與老太婆；作為誕生、成長與死亡。
I serve her in her form of Aphrodite, but she has six other manifestations which must concern you.  You will not reach the Grail unless you learn of these Six Goddesses.	我以阿芙羅黛蒂之相侍奉她，但她另有六種化身，是你必須留心的。除非你認識這六位女神，否則你到不了聖杯面前。
Six is the sacred number of Aphrodite.	六，是阿芙羅黛蒂的聖數。
It is not safe for you. You will be wise to avoid it.	那對你並不安全，避開它才是明智之舉。
There are men who know the desert and where precious water may be found, but there are men who will guide you astray so they may kill and rob you.  Be careful who you trust.	有人熟知這片沙漠、知道珍貴水源何在，但也有人會故意引你走偏，好殺你劫你。信任誰，要謹慎選擇。
It is barren, treacherous and hot as a furnace. I have known of men who cooked eggs upon the rocks at midday.	那裡荒蕪、險惡，酷熱如爐。我聽聞有人曾在正午的岩石上把雞蛋煮熟。
The Zion gate is in the southern wall of Jerusalem.	錫安城門位於耶路撒冷的南面城牆。
The Jaffa gate is in the western wall of Jerusalem and there is no fee to enter it.	賈法城門位於耶路撒冷的西面城牆，由此入城不需付費。
He is the official who runs Gaza.  He has just come to power and he hates foreigners, especially Christians.  You have escaped his notice for now, but Gaza is very dangerous for you.	他是治理加薩的官員，才剛掌權，痛恨外邦人，尤其是基督徒。目前你還沒引起他的注意，但加薩對你而言十分危險。
There is water between here and Jerusalem, but I cannot help you to find it.	此處與耶路撒冷之間確有水源，但我無法助你尋得。
Certainly, as Hazm leads you from Gaza, he will see you have a drink at a well, but that will not take you far in the desert.	當然，哈慈引你離開加薩時，會讓你在一口井邊飲水，但那點水撐不了你在沙漠裡走太遠。
The path to truth is as narrow and dangerous as a razor's edge.	通往真理之路，如刀鋒般狹窄而危險。
Though I am more than willing to answer questions, I will answer only those questions which I deem significant.	我雖十分樂意回答問題，但只會回答我認為重要的問題。
None for me, thank you.	我不用了，謝謝。
I am so glad you enjoyed my figs. What a shame there are no more.	很高興你喜歡我的無花果，可惜已經沒有了。
These are the names of the Six Goddesses: Athene, Vesta, Isis, Astarte, Ceres, Venus.	這便是六女神的名號：雅典娜、維斯塔、艾西斯、阿斯塔特、席瑞絲、維納斯。
And these are their symbols.	而這些便是她們的標識。
This is the symbol of Athene.	這是雅典娜的標識。
This is the symbol of Vesta.	這是維斯塔的標識。
This is the symbol of Isis.	這是艾西斯的標識。
This is the symbol of Astarte.	這是阿斯塔特的標識。
This is the symbol of Ceres.	這是席瑞絲的標識。
This is the symbol of Venus.	這是維納斯的標識。
There was nothing terribly interesting about that other wall.	另一面牆並沒有什麼特別值得一看的東西。
It is good that you have come.  The Captain sent word to me that you were here, though in truth I have been expecting you for some time.	你能前來，甚好。隊長已捎信告訴我你到了，其實我等候你已有些時日了。
I am Al-Sirat, the first of Six Guardians who serve the Goddess, she who gives the power of life and regeneration through her sacred cup, which you know as the Grail.	我是 Al-Sirat，六位守護女神聖杯者中的第一位。她藉由她那只聖杯——也就是你所知的聖杯——賜予生命與重生之力。
We who are the Six Guardians will test you in different ways.  We will test your mind, spirit and body.  You must pass each one of us before the Goddess will relinquish her sacred cup to you.	我們六位守護者，將以不同方式試煉你，考驗你的心智、心靈與體魄。你必須通過我們每一位，女神才會將她的聖杯交到你手中。
Excuse me, Master.  I have fed and watered the mule for your guest, as you said.	稟告主人，我已依吩咐替貴客的騾子餵食飲水了。
Thank you, Hazm.  Wait with the mule until our guest is ready to leave.  Then you will guide him in secret away from Gaza.	多謝，哈慈。你且守著騾子，等貴客準備啟程，再悄悄引他離開加薩。
I am a scholar.  I have spent my life in study and meditation.  I am at your disposal, to share what knowledge I may.	我是個學者，畢生鑽研學問、潛心冥想。但憑差遣，我所知所學，皆願與你分享。
And please, allow me to offer you qahwah to drink and figs to eat.  It is simple fare, but all that I have.	也請容我奉上卡瓦與無花果。粗茶淡飯，卻已是我所能給予的一切。
PRESS F6 WHEN FINISHED	完成後請按 F6
Here is the challenge placed before you. There are six Tablets engraved with a symbol, one for each of the Six Goddesses.	眼前便是擺在你面前的考驗。這裡有六塊刻著標識的石板，各代表六女神之一。
There are six Niches for the tablets. Choose a Niche and I will pose a question, one question for each of the Six Goddesses.	這裡有六個安放石板的壁龕。選一個壁龕，我便會提出一道問題，每位女神各有一題。
You must know which Goddess answers the question, then move the Tablet with her symbol into the Niche.	你必須判斷是哪位女神能回答這道問題，再把刻著她標識的石板移進那個壁龕。
When you have answered all six questions, only then will I tell you whether you have passed or failed.	待你答完全部六道問題，我才會告訴你，你是通過了，還是失敗了。
I bid you to begin and may Aphrodite smile upon you.	我請你開始吧，願阿芙羅黛蒂對你展露微笑。
Click on an empty Niche to see the clue.  Click on a Tablet to select it. Click on a destination to move the selected Tablet.  PRESS F6 WHEN ALL TABLETS HAVE BEEN PLACED.	點選空壁龕以查看線索。點選石板以選取它。點選目的地以移動選取的石板。所有石板都放妥後請按 F6。
USE ARROW KEYS TO POSITION CURSOR BOX.  On an empty Niche: press "Enter" to see clue.  On a Tablet: press "Enter" to select. Position cursor box on destination, and press "Enter" again to move the selected Tablet.  PRESS F6 WHEN ALL TABLETS HAVE BEEN PLACED.	用方向鍵移動游標框。停在空壁龕上：按「Enter」查看線索。停在石板上：按「Enter」選取。將游標框移至目的地，再按一次「Enter」以移動選取的石板。所有石板都放妥後請按 F6。
Your wisdom is great.  You have passed my test.	你的智慧非凡，你已通過我的試煉。
You have not passed my test. Will you try again?	你未能通過我的試煉。要再試一次嗎？
roomNum = %d	房間編號 = %d
prev room exit = %d	前一房間出口 = %d
cur room entrance = %d	目前房間入口 = %d
cur room rotation = %d	目前房間旋轉角度 = %d
My King! You have won the Grail!	吾王！您已贏得聖杯！
Aye, but rise, Sir Galahad, and draw near to your King at once! A great power is at work!	正是，但快起身，葛拉漢爵士，速速上前見你的王！一股偉大的力量正在運作！
The Grail has chosen to bring you home in your hour of desperate need!	在你危急存亡之際，聖杯選擇帶你回家！
The Grail has brought you here, Arthur. Only one god may rule in thy kingdom now. The altar of the Christ god awaits its vessel.	聖杯帶你來到此處，亞瑟。如今你的王國只能容一位神祇為主。基督之神的祭壇，正等候著承接它的聖器。
Cast down your eyes! The radiance of the Grail is too great for any man to see.	垂下你的雙眼！聖杯的光輝太過耀眼，凡人不可直視。
Behold, Mithra has been driven away! And the Grail is gone!	看啊，米夏拉已被驅逐！聖杯也已消失無蹤！
It has become a healing force that spreads outward, touching every corner of your kingdom!	它已化作一股治癒之力向外擴散，觸及你王國的每一個角落！
The land returns to life. The lakes and rivers and wells fill once more with clean, fresh water.	這片土地重獲新生。湖泊、河流與水井再度盈滿潔淨甘美的水。
Camelot is healed!	肯萊特痊癒了！
You receive Gwenhyver's praise and adoration, as you have well earned.	你得到了昆海兒的讚美與愛慕，這是你應得的。
Your knights salute you and the joyous cries of the love and      gratitude of your people fills          the air.	你的騎士向你致敬，人民滿懷愛戴與      感恩的歡呼聲，迴盪在          空中。
And so you have won, through purity of spirit and heart, through skill and strength. No praise is too great.	如此，你已然勝利——憑藉心靈與靈魂的純淨，憑藉技藝與力量。任何讚譽，都不足以言表。
With peace and prosperity returned to your kingdom, you have the time to rest and enjoy the land you have saved.	隨著和平與繁榮重返你的王國，你終於有時間歇息，享受你所拯救的這片土地。
But though your land is healed, your heart is not. Perhaps it never shall be.	然而，縱使你的國土已然痊癒，你的心卻未曾痊癒。或許，永遠也不會痊癒。
FINIS	劇終
